title: Education & Science
new-page: true
is-card: true
on-arrival: education_science_timer += 9; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/portraits/kmtedu.jpg
go-to: ed_menu
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

# options:
# - fund research (basic science research at the KWI, medical research, applied and industrial research to benefit Germany's economy)
# - change the educational curriculum (only once per 3 years) - will have a "major" and "minor" option:
# - democratic education - focus on critical thinking and democratic values rather than authoritarian teaching. (+ democratization, pro_republic)
# - scientific education - focus on the sciences, mathematics, and technical skills (+ NMC, science)
# - humanistic education - focus on literature, history, and philosophy. (+ NMC, pro_republic if democratization is high)
# - traditional education (reduces relations with DDP)

# - increase educational opportunities for working-class families.
# - Secularize education (+ DVP, instant Zentrum vonc)

# source for some of the education stuff: Martin, G. W. “Educational Reform in Germany 1918-1933.” Masters, Durham University, 1972. https://etheses.dur.ac.uk/9738/.

# Forman, Paul. “The Financial Support and Political Alignment of Physicists in Weimar Germany.” Minerva 12, no. 1 (1974): 39–66.

# science increases economic growth...

= Education and Science

Education in Germany is an area of mixed responsibility between the state governments and the central government. The Weimar Constitution claims that schools are the domain of the central government, but in practice much of it is left to the states, as the Reichstag has historically been unable to pass an education law. Currently, with our control of Prussia and the Chancellorship, we can try to set policy for a large part of the country.

[? if major_curriculum: Current educational curriculum - [+ major_curriculum +], [+ minor_curriculum +] ?]

@ed_menu
view-if: not last_advisor_action

- @increase_education
- @structure
- @curriculum
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action


@increase_education
title: Increase funding for schools in China.

China is still backwards. We must teach the people to build a better society for all.

- @schoolbuild
- @schoolsupplies
- @medical
- @cut_funding
- @ed_menu: Do not increase research funding.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@schoolbuild
title: Fund building schools in the countryside.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; education += 1; economic_growth += 0.3; if economic_growth <= 8; unemployed -= 0.2; if unemployed >= 4; west_relation += 1; rural_kmt += 3;

Building schools in rural areas increases our popular support as well as their education.

@schoolsupplies
title: Fund school supplies to existing schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; education += 1; economic_growth += 0.5 if economic_growth <= 8; and applied_research <= 1; economic_growth += 3 if applied_research > 1; new_middle_kmt += 5*(1-dissent); workers_kmt += 3*(1-dissent);

Giving more supplies to existing schools provide them with more means to learn and think.

@medical
title: Fund biomedical research at the hospitals and medical schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; education += 1; economic_growth += 0.4 if economic_growth <= 8; new_middle_kmt += 5*(1-dissent); workers_kmt += 3*(1-dissent);unemployed -= 0.2 if unemployed >= 4;

Our research program focuses on medical research to improve the treatment of diseases and public health.

@cut_funding
title: Cut science funding.
subtitle: +1 budget
choose-if: science_funding >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have not funded science.
on-arrival: budget += 1; education -= 1; economic_growth -= 0.5; new_middle_kmt -= 5; workers_kmt -= 2; unemployed += 0.3

We have cut funding for science. This has a negative effect on our economic growth, and the advancement of our society.

@structure
title: Change the structure and funding of education.

Education in China has traditionally been organized on religious and class lines. In addition, the working class has at most eight years of public education in primary and middle schools, while the middle and upper classes have access to private schools and Gymnasiums that prepare students for universities. Thus, the universities tend to be dominated by conservatives and reactionaries, which has negative consequences for bureaucratic recruitment.

- @westerniza
- @public_hs
- @propaganda
- @ed_menu: Do not change school funding or organization.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@westernize
title: Support organizing schools more on Western systems.
on-arrival: education += 1; west_relations += 1; new_middle_kmt += 3;

More schools are now operating on Western systems instead of Japanese ones.

@public_hs
title: Increase educational opportunities for the working class by funding public high schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; workers_kmt += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); education += 0.5; unemployed -= 0.2; economic_growth += 0.2; pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent);
max-visits: 3

# this makes the bureaucracy more proletarian
We have funded more public secondary schools so that proletarian children may receive the same education as middle and upper-class children, and can be prepared for universities.

@propaganda
title: Add our propaganda campaigns as part of the curriculum.
on-arrival: workers_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_kmt += 2*(1-dissent); pro_republic += 5;

We have oriented schools to spread our message further.

@curriculum
title: Change the educational curriculum.
choose-if: curriculum_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if curriculum_timer > 0 : It is too early to change the curriculum again. ?]

Many intellectuals believe that education in China is not fit for the modern era. Much of the educational system still follows imperial-era traditions of militaristic discipline, and far-right professors and students rule the universities. Nevertheless, there have been strides in bringing poor children into the schools.

What should be the major focus of our new curriculum?

- @dem_major
- @science_major
- @human_major
- @vocational_major
- @trad_major
- @ed_menu: Do not change the curriculum now.
- @cancel_advisor_action

# note: education_science is a variable that affects how much education affects economic growth.

@dem_major
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
view-if: major_curriculum != "democratic"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "democratic"; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); workers_kmt += 2*(1-dissent);

We should teach students how to be citizens of a democratic republic, by teaching them about our idea of Political Tutelage and the road to restoring democracy.

@science_major
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Modern science, mathematics, and technical skills
view-if: major_curriculum != "scientific"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "scientific"; education += 0.5; new_middle_kmt += 2*(1-dissent); workers_kmt += 2*(1-dissent)

Our educational system should reflect the modern age, and we should teach science and rational thinking. Religious conservatives tend to react negatively against this. 

@human_major
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
view-if: major_curriculum != "humanist"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "humanist"; new_middle_kmt += 3*(1-dissent);

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history, and philosophy. Some criticize this curriculum as focusing too much on "useless" subjects, while others worry that the arts establishment is too closely tied to romantic nationalism.

@vocational_major
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Useful technical skills for future careers
view-if: major_curriculum != "vocational"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "vocational"; education_science += 0.3; workers_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_kmt += 2*(1-dissent);

Education should be focused on providing a useful hands-on education, and teach the skills that will be most useful for students' future lives.

@trad_major
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Classics, discipline, and nationalism
view-if: major_curriculum != "traditional"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "traditional"; old_middle_kmt += 2*(1-dissent); rural_kmt += 2*(1-dissent); pro_republic -= 3

The traditional curriculum had a focus on ancient history and language, as well as traditional Confuscian ideals.

@curriculum_minor

And what should be a secondary focus of the curriculum?

- @dem_minor
- @science_minor
- @human_minor
- @vocational_minor
- @trad_minor

@dem_minor
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
view-if: major_curriculum != "democratic"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "democratic"; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); workers_kmt += 2*(1-dissent); democratization += 1; z_relation -= 2; dvp_relation -= 3;

We should teach students how to be citizens of a democratic republic, by teaching them to critically evaluate politics and current events, to exercise their rights and to respect the rights of other citizens. Traditionalists of all stripes are critical of this curriculum.

@science_minor
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Modern science, mathematics, and technical skills
view-if: major_curriculum != "scientific"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 0.5; z_relation -= 3; ddp_relation += 3*(1-dissent); kpd_relation += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_kmt += 2*(1-dissent); workers_kmt += 2*(1-dissent)

Our educational system should reflect the modern age, and we should teach science and rational thinking. Religious conservatives tend to react negatively against this. 

@human_minor
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
view-if: major_curriculum != "humanist"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "humanist"; new_middle_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); ddp_relation += 3*(1-dissent);

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history, and philosophy. Some criticize this curriculum as focusing too much on "useless" subjects, while others worry that the arts establishment is too closely tied to romantic nationalism.

@vocational_minor
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Useful technical skills for future careers
view-if: major_curriculum != "vocational"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "vocational"; education_science += 0.3; workers_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_kmt += 2*(1-dissent);

Education should be focused on providing a useful hands-on education, and teach the skills that will be most useful for students' future lives.


@trad_minor
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Classics, discipline, and nationalism
view-if: major_curriculum != "traditional"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "traditional"; old_middle_kmt += 2*(1-dissent); rural_kmt += 2*(1-dissent); pro_republic -= 3

The traditional curriculum had a focus on ancient history and language, as well as traditional Confuscian ideals.


